{"name":"Dreyfus","hex":"#b2aba1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Dreyfus","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Dreyfus"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dreyfus (surname)","blocks":[{"text":"Dreyfus is a surname of German origin. Notable people with the surname include:"}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dreyfus_(surname)"},{"title":"Dreyfus affair","blocks":[{"text":"The Dreyfus affair was a political scandal that divided the Third French Republic from 1894 until its resolution in 1906. The scandal began in December 1894 when Captain Alfred Dreyfus, a 35-year-old Alsatian French artillery officer of Jewish descent, was wrongfully convicted of treason for communicating French military secrets to the German Embassy in Paris. He was sentenced to life imprisonment and sent overseas to the penal colony on Devil's Island in French Guiana, where he spent the following five years imprisoned in very harsh conditions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Alfred_Dreyfus_%281859-1935%29_-_photo_originale.jpg/330px-Alfred_Dreyfus_%281859-1935%29_-_photo_originale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dreyfus_affair"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Degradation_alfred_dreyfus.jpg/500px-Degradation_alfred_dreyfus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Degradation_alfred_dreyfus.jpg/1280px-Degradation_alfred_dreyfus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Degradation_alfred_dreyfus.jpg/500px-Degradation_alfred_dreyfus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fil